  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Peter''s stepped-up basis under Section 1014 is $175,000 (FMV at date of death). His gain is $185,000 - $175,000 = $10,000. Although Peter held the land only three months, inherited property is automatically treated as long-term regardless of the actual holding period. The $135,000 of appreciation during the grandmother''s lifetime is eliminated by the step-up.
Wrong (B): $10,000 short-term capital gain incorrectly treats the gain as short-term; inherited property is deemed held long-term regardless of actual holding period under Section 1223(9).
Wrong (C): $145,000 incorrectly uses the grandmother''s original cost basis ($40,000) instead of the stepped-up basis ($175,000).
Wrong (D): While the $10,000 gain amount and long-term character are correctly computed, inherited property receives a stepped-up basis, making the gain $10,000, not calculated from the original cost.$EXPL$
