  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under the residual method of IRC Section 1060, the purchase price of a business is first allocated to identifiable tangible and intangible assets at FMV. Any excess ($800,000 - $700,000 = $100,000) is allocated to goodwill, a Section 197 intangible amortized over 15 years.
Wrong (A): The excess cannot be added to the building''s basis because the building has already been allocated its full FMV of $300,000 under Section 1060.
Wrong (B): Similarly, equipment has already received its full FMV allocation of $200,000; additional basis cannot be assigned arbitrarily.
Wrong (D): Goodwill is a Section 197 intangible, not a Section 1231 asset. Section 1231 applies to depreciable business property and real property held more than one year.$EXPL$
