-- Q2557: Property Transactions: Basis [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under Treas. Reg. Section 1.167(g)-1, when personal-use property is converted to business use, the depreciable basis is the lower of adjusted basis ($35,000) or FMV at conversion ($22,000). Since FMV is lower, the depreciable basis is $22,000. This prevents depreciation deductions for the $13,000 personal-use decline.
Wrong (A): $35,000 is the original cost, but using it would allow Carol to claim depreciation on the $13,000 decline that occurred during personal use.
Wrong (C): $28,500 (the midpoint of cost and FMV) has no basis in tax law; the rule requires the lower of the two amounts, not an average.
Wrong (D): $13,000 is the personal-use decline in value ($35,000 - $22,000), not the depreciable basis.$EXPL$
