  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under Section 1015, the donee''s basis in gifted property is the donor''s carryover basis of $45,000. Because FMV equals the donor''s basis, the dual-basis rule does not apply and there is no built-in gain or loss. Dan''s holding period also tacks onto the donor''s under Section 1223(2).
Wrong (A): A $0 basis has no support in Section 1015. Gifted property always carries over the donor''s basis (or uses FMV for loss purposes when FMV is lower).
Wrong (B): The basis is determinable — it is simply the donor''s carryover basis of $45,000. There is no ambiguity when FMV equals the donor''s basis.
Wrong (C): $22,500 (half of basis) has no basis in tax law. Section 1015 does not reduce the carryover basis by any fraction.$EXPL$
