-- Q2566: Property Transactions: Gains/Losses [easy/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under IRC Section 1231(a)(2), a net Section 1231 loss is treated as an ordinary loss, fully deductible against the taxpayer''s ordinary income without limitation. This favorable treatment is a key benefit of Section 1231 — gains are treated as long-term capital gains, but losses receive ordinary loss treatment.
Wrong (A): The $3,000 annual deduction limit under Section 1211(b) applies only to capital losses, not to ordinary losses from Section 1231.
Wrong (C): Section 1231 ordinary losses are currently deductible and are not carried forward indefinitely. Capital loss carryforward rules do not apply.
Wrong (D): The equipment was held for more than one year, so any loss would be long-term, not short-term. Moreover, the loss is ordinary under Section 1231, not capital.$EXPL$
